Mechs:
------

Your mech is your best friend. treat it with respect and it will save your
life, but misuse it and beware!

Mechs come in all different shapes and sizes, primarily:

Small - 5 ton frame, these are fast mechs, but dont carry much and are limited
        by the energy it can carry due to lack of shielding

Medium - 20 ton frame, these are your best bet, they hold more energy and
         have the ability to use slotcards, a valuable asset.

Large - Strictly for the heavy hitters, a 50 ton frame, slow moving behemoth,
        able to survive more battles, carries more and such.

NOTE: Custom mechs can be created at PRIMUC, strictly black market.


Following report on mech accessory hardware.

Armor:

Armor can easily be replaced at the Dexxon City.


Energy:

Energy is used by your mech for everything.  Solar rechargers refuel you
nightly, but more can be purchased at Dexxon City


Jato Jets:

These allow you to jump over sectors and aid in battle.


Battery Booster:

This daily option will turbo charge your power plant, allowing mechs to
move faster.


Cloaking Shield:

A daily option that will render you invisible to ALL.


Slotcards:

These can be used only one at a time, but can be switched out.

o Mine scanner - reports vorpal mines near you
o Mech scanner - reports other mechs near you
o Terrain viewer - Reports acid lakes near you
o Ore Identifier - Reports ore near you
o 1 Shot City Teleport - used once, it signals the city teleporters to get you
o Radar System - A bad black market copy of Enhanced radar. but it works!
o Enhanced Radar - A radar system that reports visually (A Pirate best Buy!)
o AutoModem - A black market 9600 baud modem for your mech

Mech Computer Systems:

General:

the main mech computer allows you to access several things

o Cyberlink mail - send or recieve mail to other mechs
o Robo droids - remote linkup to recon
o Locate Commodities - Recalls from memory locations of FORTS and Mining pods
o AutoDrive - Lets you pilot your mech over long distances
o Slotcard storage - Allows you to switch slotcards in the field
o Automodem Commands - Remote access of Forts and City Mainframe

Battle:

the battle computer is important in battle

o SDI [on/off] - Set to off if you want to attack mechs that approach you
                 (Note: this is for when you are NOT playing the game!)

o TBO [install/reprogram] - This allows you to program a sequence of
                 battle moves for greater killing power.


CelSigns:

A Celsign is simply a signpost you plant into the ground


Weapons:
-------

Hand:

There are several types of hand weapons availible to you in the city store.
all can be used for mining of ore.

Long Range:

The only known LR weapon is black market, called a flux shell launcher.
Flux shells adonize armor, thus they cannot harm you, but can wreck your
mech in a hurry.

Vorpal mines:

These are deadly!  First they explode, damaging your mech slightly, then 
they set up a vorpal shock wave inside your mech, damaging you.




Dexxon City:
-----------

Dexxon is the founder of the planet, having repelled the pirate horde
that once claimed it, they have recruited you to mine ore for them.

The City consists of several shops:

o Garths mech repair - Buy armor, energy and a healing Yanis patch
o Drogs - Slotcard city! also sells other items.
o Rabbles - Old Rabble will let you use his recon droids
o Dexxon - We buy ores from you and have a variety of pods availible (see below)
o HUD - general contractors for FORTS (see below)
o Mainframe - A computer you can access for various info
o Soothsayer - ???????


Pods:

o Defence - will defend a sector against anything - heat activated
o Mining - will mine a sector for you - no defence
o Sensor - transmits info thru telemetry on mechs that pass over it


Pirate City:
-----------

Little is known about this haven for the black market, not even its location
(which can change)  PRIMUC is located there, discounted shops.


Fortresses:
----------

HUD will build you a variety of Forts, from a standard fort, to a garrison.
These buildings survive your own mechs destruction and serve as a storehouse
for various things like armor, fluxshells, etc.  Your own personal bank is located
here.  The larger of these buildings actually staff techs that create items for you.
But Beware! If your funds in the bank run out, so does production.


